-- title:
--   Type-preserving quaternion units have even reduced-norm valuation
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ be a prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $r$ in the sense that $r$ is a nonunit of $A$, and let $\mathrm{ratClosure}\,A$ denote the topological closure of the prime subfield inside the completion of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at the valuation of $A$. Let $R_0$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, equipped with an algebra structure making $\mathrm{ratClosure}\,A$ its fraction field, and assume that the image of $R_0$ in $\mathrm{ratClosure}\,A$ consists exactly of those elements whose valuation in the completion is at most $1$. Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$, let $\iota$ be an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra homomorphism from the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ to $M_2(\mathrm{ratClosure}\,A)$, and let $\rho\colon \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]^{\times}\to \mathrm{PGL}_2(\mathrm{ratClosure}\,A)$ be the monoid homomorphism sending a unit $x$ to the projective class of the invertible matrix $\iota(x)$. Assume $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]^{\times}$ acts on the set of homothety classes of full $R_0$-lattices in $(\mathrm{ratClosure}\,A)^2$ so that the action of each $g$ coincides with the action of $\rho(g)$. Then for a unit $x$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ the following are equivalent: (i) $x$ belongs to the subgroup of elements $g$ such that, in the graph on lattice classes with adjacency generated by adjacency of representing lattices, the distance mod $2$ from the class of the standard lattice $R_0^2$ to $g\cdot w$ equals that to $w$ for every vertex $w$; (ii) $\mathrm{padicValRat}_r$ of $\mathrm{nrd}(x) = x_{\mathrm{re}}^2 - a\,x_{I}^2 - b\,x_{J}^2 + ab\,x_{K}^2$ is even.
--
--   This identifies the type-preserving subgroup of a rational quaternion unit group acting on the Bruhat–Tits tree of $\mathrm{PGL}_2$ over the $r$-adic closure with the subgroup $\Gamma_+$ of elements of even reduced-norm valuation, the standard normalisation in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd description of Shimura curves. It is obtained from the general criterion in terms of the valuation of the determinant of a representing matrix, and is used in the results on descent and on permutations of quotient vertices and edges.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_BruhatTits_mem_typePreserving_iff_even_padicValRat_nrd.lean

